---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About an aerospace and mechanical engineer focused on traceable analysis, hardware, verification, and communication."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell page-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="page-hero-index">01 / PROFILE</span>
        <h1>Engineering at the boundary of analysis and hardware.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="page-hero-note">
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad">
    <div class="shell about-intro-grid">
      <aside class="about-aside">
        <dl>
          <div>
            <dt>Education</dt>
            <dd>Aerospace Engineering <br />
                Mechanical Engineering <br />
                Applied Physics
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Location</dt>
            <dd>{site.location}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Working style</dt>
            <dd>Analytical <br />
                Collaborative <br />
                Hardware Focus
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Portfolio scope</dt>
            <dd>Sanitized public examples</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </aside>

      <div class="prose-large">
        <p class="eyebrow">Profile</p>
        <h2>I thrive making complicated systems legible.</h2>
        <p>
          My experience and education have provided me the opportunity to hone my passion of solving
          complex problems with clear and concise documentation. When a problem arises I derive explicit requirements,
          bound assumptions, observable evidence, and a mathematical model to represent each case. With all this clearly
          displayed, my engineering team can make reasonable and informed decisions. 
        </p>
        <p>
          There is always room to grow and I am learning new methods, decision consequences, and _____ every day, 
          but I feel like I am reaching the plateu of mechanical hardware development growth. I want to continue this path
          of exponential growth by transitioning into nuclear fusion work. I am looking for a highly technical role 
          with complex analytical and mechanical physics problems to solve, and contributing to electricity generation 
          with today's energy crisis appeals to my motivations. 
        </p>
        <p>
          The content in this portfolio is intended to provide evidence of my abilities in this transition. Beyond education and
          description of my roles, this portfolio contains representative sub-projects, tools, and writings. Program names,
          organizations, numerical results, and proprietary details are omitted unless approved public material is available.
          Approved material pertaining to my work is displayed in the 'News' page.
        </p>
        <p>
          Personally; I love nature photography and exploring through hikes. This world is filled with interesting systems
          and getting to observe them while practicing making assumption is a lot of fun. Cloud systems, rock structures, 
          ecology of bugs in the desert. They all follow the same physical principles that we use to develop space hardware
          or generate fusion, just in different levels and interesting methods. 
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

   </BaseLayout>
